so much happened so quickly we can all  agree cgi is a marvel movie's best  friend dr strange in the multiverse of  madness takes that concept to the next  level using a ton of visual effects so  let's hop through the portal and take a  look at those impressive scenes  number one if you didn't like this movie  for whatever reason we think you can  agree with us that this scene was pretty  amazing as doctor strange grabs america  into a multiverse portal they fall  through the most random universes of  course there's not a whole lot of  practical things vfx artists could have  done here so this scene had to be  completely cgi we would have thought  there'd at least be the actors in front  of a blue screen but those close-ups on  benedict cumberbatch were all  convincingly digital the process to make  this moment was very tedious for artists  as they had to make each environment  more unique than the last pretty  impressive stuff here but the real  madness comes from those couple of  scenes in the paint reality  professionals that are in visual effects  can tell you how difficult it is to work  with liquid physics i think the whole  thing was challenging because there's so  many elements that go from shot to shot  number two only doctor strange could  concoct a trap fit enough to distract an  evil witch but don't be fooled here this  moment was entirely digital unlike our  last entry production coordinators did  indeed have the real elizabeth olsen  here but that was as real as it gets the  only real behind the scenes look we have  here is an amazing looking contraption  spinning around olson as she stands in  front of a backdrop  as simple as that was to shoot producing  the mirror environment around her was a  whole other feat  number three the opening of any movie  needs to be able to grab the audience's  attention and as multiverse of madness  begins so does the maddening cgi work  for vfx artists the whole environment  produced in the scene was 100 digital  set designers built a massive green  sound stage and a little strip for the  actors to sprint down  number four why not include a little  demon fight in a sam raimi horror film  as strange attempts to dreamwalk into  zombie strange christine now has to  complete the mission every common gamer  loathes protect the hero until the timer  runs out now knowing that it would be  pretty dangerous for the director to  include real-life demon bats rachel  mcadams had to beef up her cgi chops and  fight with the air  number five a broken reality needs a lot  of cgi to fix it back up in the scene  where strange and christine find  themselves trapped in a broken reality  everything is quite literally turned on  its side artists had a lot of background  work to get done in order to make up the  chaos some practical pieces were added  like the floating car and building  structures it must have been a real  change for the vfx team to actually get  permission to go as wild and unexplained  as possible here  number six it takes a while for some  people to get with the digital craze and  for some of the members of the  illuminati they went full cgi with their  outfits surprisingly the suits reed  richards and black bolt dawned were  entirely digital to get the task done  vfx coordinators crafted skin tight  suits covered in trackers to make sure  the digital makeup stayed put on their  bodies but the work doesn't end there  the big fight scene against the scarlet  witch was not even done with all the  actors in the same room we don't know if  it was due to scheduling or the pandemic  but they basically had only two to three  actors communicating in real time on set  we wanted the fans to go oh how cool  number seven you've gotta keep both eyes  open for this one especially if you're  cumberbatch or you'll miss nothing on  set in terms of cg monsters this beast  was very well done if only the actors  could have seen it in real life stun  coordinators had to work endlessly with  the vfx team in order to make sure  everything matched up adding as much  practicality as possible before anything  got too dangerous or destructive on set  number 8. possessing a zombie is a  little extreme for a marvel movie but if  you hire sam raimi to direct nothing's  too extreme for the zombie scene set  designers built a massive stage with  blue backdrops and a really impressive  cliff as filming on location for that  scene would have been dangerous they  went for as much digital here as  possible not just on the environment but  even zombie strange got a bit of work  done on his face in post-production i  wanted that character  to have conflict  number nine the space between realities  needed to look as trippy as possible so  no use of practical effects were  necessary here all of this is pure cgi  with the help of a few actors to sell  the scene it's fitting for an  environment between realities to really  have no sense of reality at all  number 10 you know we're all about that  cgi cape no practical if that little  joke flew by your heads no worries maybe  let strange's cape do the explaining  since a lot of what our hero does is  with a flying and somewhat conscious  cape it'll need a whole lot of digital  and in this case it looks like even when  he was stationary the cape was not made  practically there are a lot of moments  on set where we can see benedict  strolling around with one over his  shoulders so it's super cool that they  keep us guessing when it's real or not  number 11 look at all those layers when  america was able to punch like a  superhero it always made for a pretty  stunning visual effects artist really  broke down the visual of the punch  adding on layers and layers putting the  super in superhero punch this one in  particular was a little more tedious  because of the fact that america was  punching a glass like cell but at this  point shattering glass effects are a  no-brainer for these professionals to  achieve  number 12. talk about catfishing a  sorcerer when the scarlet witch reveals  her true evil colors to strange the  entire environment becomes void of all  life the light is taken away to reveal  an evil red landscape not that this was  the most difficult effect to achieve or  anything but this was super interesting  to see behind the scenes by just adding  a touch of red and throwing the actors  in front of a backdrop they were able to  change the tone of the scene almost  effortlessly sometimes you just gotta  take the digital shortcut and with  marvel vfx artists they deserve a few  breaks every once in a while  number 13 benedict stop hitting yourself  stop hitting yourself when a scene calls  for two different versions of an actor  to interact with each other the most  simple way of doing it is just splitting  them up on the frame for different takes  but fighting each other with close-ups  not so simple with the spells being a  big factor vfx artists now had to  seamlessly match up the cgi needed to  fill in the scene's environment luckily  production hired a stunt double to  execute it more practically but getting  those moments synced up effectively is  all thanks to those editors and cgi  artists  number 14 if you've watched some of our  previous doctor strange videos you'll  know that the siege of carmitage was  definitely the heftiest one on  production all those different sound  stages were built perfectly to coincide  with each other however none of this  could have been held together without a  little digital glue all the magic spells  and environments were executed in post  blending in with the practical sets and  lighting without each of these aspects  working hand in hand this scene would  have not turned out the way it did it  was a great collaboration between  special effects stunts camera crews  number 15 wanda is no stranger to  creating imaginary worlds but she  couldn't have done this one without a  little help from cgi while a lot of the  dark hold is indeed practical there are  always bits of the environment that need  a little digital touch up artists worked  on the background of this one a lot  adding in a few spell effects as well  it's hard to believe cgi sometimes but  marvel has only proved how far that  technology has come with the rollout of  multiverse of madness so put on those  imagination capes if you were in a  marvel movie what's the one effect you'd  want the artist to do to you let us know  in the comments
 

